# Build context for the service images in deploy/docker/.
#
# Scope rule, learned the hard way: exclude only what is provably huge and
# provably not a build input. "Probably not needed by the build" is not a
# safe assumption in this repository.
#
# The first version of this file excluded `docs/` and `*.md`. That broke
# the gm-console image on its very first CI run:
#
#   error: couldn't read `crates/gm-console/src/../../../docs/commercial/TERMS.md`
#   error: couldn't read `crates/gm-console/src/../../../docs/commercial/PRIVACY.md`
#   error: could not compile `gm-console` (lib) due to 2 previous errors
#
# `routes.rs` reaches out of the crate with `include_str!` for six files:
#
#   LICENSE                                 (the /license endpoint)
#   docs/commercial/TERMS.md                (the /terms endpoint)
#   docs/commercial/PRIVACY.md              (the /privacy endpoint)
#   apps/gm-console-web/dist/robots.txt
#   apps/gm-console-web/dist/sitemap.xml
#   apps/gm-console-web/dist/index.html     (the SPA fallback)
#
# A local `cargo build` cannot see any of that, because the files are right
# there. Only a build from a filtered context fails, which is exactly what
# the container build is. So: exclude the big, boring, provably-unused
# things, and leave the rest of the tree alone.

# Build output. Many GB on a developer machine, and a different set of
# hashes than the container will produce anyway. The build stage uses a
# cache mount for this, which keeps the useful part of the cache without
# needing any of it in the context.
target/
**/target/

# Local scratch lanes and version-control metadata.
worktrees/
.worktrees/
.git/
.github/

# Editor / OS noise.
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
